A court of fey holds a glade deep in the [[Verdant Expanse]], where the forest is permanently dark. They are tall and gangly, with bluish-gray skin and limbs stretched longer than a person's. They wrap themselves in sheer gossamer cloth that looks too fine to have been made. Their faces are not faces: a bony growth covers the front of the head like a fused mask, and it opens to speak with a circular, lamprey-like mouth. Two horns rise from the top of the mask, and where eyes would be are empty black holes.

Their leader speaks of a Lady they serve, whose court lies beyond a door. The two who held court in the glade were [[People/Oriel|Oriel]], who played a harp, and [[People/Jin|Jin]], who spoke for the rest. Smaller ones sat in a ring around them and were called courtiers. A black raiment hangs over the two leaders, unlike any raiment of the Outer Gods the investigators knew, and unlike the green of the [[Green Father]].

They do not use names much among themselves and think the small folk give them out too freely. They knew of the Green Father as something the "silly little ones outside" worship. They said a man passing through their wastes could have come and gone without their knowing him.

The court offered the investigators a choice: to entreat their Lady and end the curse, or to have the curse pointed at people of their choosing. To end it they would have to enter the court through a door in a fallen tree, and Jin said that entering would mean forsaking the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]], and that they would die. Oriel played a song and a rectangular door carved itself into the bark of the trunk behind her, marked with a crescent moon.

The investigators refused the door and attacked. Oriel and Jin and the courtiers were all killed.
